WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
Think about this: Which communication is
appropriate?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:04.860
Let’s work through it together.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.540
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 16: Run a
permissioned consultation.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.800
Begin with identity and permission: who
you are, why the person requested

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.640
the conversation, and what they want help
understanding.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.000
State that you are not the custodian and
cannot promise a disbursement.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.020
Keep the explanation grounded in the
source documents available for that

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.720
authorized file. A neutral example is:
“You asked us to help organize your

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.840
documents. The record we have is dated
this month and describes a deposit.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.300
We have not yet verified the remaining
balance or entitlement.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.520
The official office explains the direct
process here.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.600
Would you like a list of the missing
documents for your review?” This is a

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.060
fictional practice script, not permission
to contact strangers.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:55.120
Avoid pressure based on fear, a fabricated
deadline, or a claim of

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.240
exclusivity. If a real deadline may exist,
identify its source and refer the

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.940
legal timing question promptly.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.220
Ask what the person understood before
discussing any locally reviewed

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.340
service terms. Pause and try this.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.400
Role-play a consultation using fictional
facts.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.560
Include one confirmed fact, two unknowns,
the direct-claim route, and a

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.740
specific next action. Quick knowledge
check.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.060
Which communication is appropriate?

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.500
The answer: Here is what the dated source
says and what remains unverified.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:33.540
Communicate verified facts and limits
without pressure or false authority.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.000
Keep the source, the date, and the
unknowns visible.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:38.720
I'll see you in the next lesson.
